The zuhtml package bundles a copy of the Gumbo HTML5 parser. zuhtml is
distributed under the MIT license and Gumbo under the Apache License,
Version 2.0. The two licences apply to their respective files; the package
as a whole is not MIT-licensed.


zuhtml
======

Copyright (c) 2026 Pedro Baltazar

Covers everything in the package except src/vendor/. Full text in
LICENSE.md in the source repository; CRAN's YEAR/COPYRIGHT HOLDER form is
in LICENSE.


Gumbo
=====

Bundled in src/vendor/gumbo/.

Copyright 2010, 2011 Google Inc.

Apache License, Version 2.0. Full text in src/vendor/gumbo/COPYING.
src/vendor/gumbo/utf8.c also contains a UTF-8 decoder copyright (c)
2008-2009 Bjoern Hoehrmann under the MIT license; its notice is in that
file and in inst/COPYRIGHTS. Upstream is
https://codeberg.org/gumbo-parser/gumbo-parser, and the pinned release, its
commit, its checksum and the import date are recorded in
src/vendor/PROVENANCE.

The tree is upstream's files plus exactly the local patch series listed in
src/vendor/PROVENANCE: a parse-time nesting-depth limit, the removal of the
library's only printf(), and the modification notices Apache-2.0 requires.
Each modified file says so under its licence header. The script that proves
the tree is upstream plus those patches, tools/verify-vendor, is not part of
the distributed package; it and the patches live in the source repository
at <https://github.com/pedrobtz/zuhtml>.

Only the parser library is bundled. Gumbo's Python bindings, tests,
benchmarks, examples, fuzzers and build systems are not included.
